WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:01.100
(Kelly screaming)

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.760
- So we always want to be
sure that you end this hour

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.680
with a little bit more
joy, you're welcome.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.851
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:06.851 --> 00:00:09.830
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.030
Lots of people would shudder at the idea

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.080
of living in a tiny house.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.910
Those are usually about 225
square feet and on some land,

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.290
but now a guy on TikTok is
showing off his small digs

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.970
and it's even tinier than that.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.230
It's a 95 square foot
apartment in New York City.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.430
Check this out.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.893
- Wherever your expectations
are, lower them.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:33.290
(door creaking)

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.920
As soon as you walk in the door,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.770
we have the sink.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.950
Right next to the sink, is
conveniently located the kitchen.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.870
Pantry is absolutely stocked.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.720
I have two beds, but only one me.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.870
Some nights, I'm a queen guy,

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.880
other nights I chill on the twin.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.270
Closet, that's the whole place.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.420
- Oh my God I wish I could say

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.000
what Chris just said
on TV, that's amazing.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.700
He is certainly making the
most of what he's got y'all,

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.533
this is amazing.

00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:00.240
And we have him on the line right now.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.493
What's up Axel.

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:03.830
- Hi Kelly.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.830
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.370
So how do you come to
live in that apartment?

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.050
Like, how much do you have to,

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.300
I don't know if this is a rude question,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.490
but I feel like New
York City is so pricey.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.330
How much are you paying
for that apartment?

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.070
- New York City is pricey

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.410
and the story of how I
got it begins like this.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.060
I was working in Michigan
just about two months ago

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.770
and I had a job that I
wasn't super passionate about

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.130
and as I was sitting there at
my desk, I thought to myself,

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.630
I can be anywhere and
I can become anything

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:32.882
and I believe that's true for everyone.

00:01:32.882 --> 00:01:33.960
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.530
- So I decided, where do I want to be?

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:36.850
I said, New York City.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.030
I packed my bags in my
car and I came here.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.340
Now this apartment
wasn't ready right away,

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.320
so I spent roughly three weeks

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.150
parked in a Walmart parking lot.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:49.200
Like imagine not being able
to fully stretch out your legs

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.760
and then moving into here
on a queen size mattress

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.410
where I can fully stretch out
and enjoy the comfort of AC,

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.020
so this is a major upgrade.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.920
The price is 1200 a month.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.750
- What!
- But I give you

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.190
right there on the street.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.560
Did you just scream?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.187
- Yes.

00:02:05.187 --> 00:02:07.410
- I'm right here in New
York, I get to walk outside,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.480
I get to feel the buzz
of the city around me.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.680
So it's 1200, but I get the
energy and the community.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.160
- Okay, I love where you're
at, but when you do upgrade,

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.560
you got to come back on our show

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.360
because I wanna see what your
next apartment looks like.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.970
- I would absolutely, I would love to,

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.070
I'd love to come on again.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.500
And I have to say, before
we go, I'm a huge fan.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.530
While I was driving here,

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.340
it was actually one of
the songs I listened to.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.448
Making the way from
Michigan in New York City.

00:02:30.448 --> 00:02:31.564
♪ Since you've been gone ♪

00:02:31.564 --> 00:02:32.397
- I love it.

00:02:32.397 --> 00:02:35.060
♪ I can breathe for the first time ♪

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.490
- I love it.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.720
Thank you so much Axel, we love you,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.400
I'm liking your posts right now, right?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.300
- Thank you.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.480
- Okay, well, that's not all.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.940
Our season long partner,
Pilot pen makers of G2

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.840
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.250
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.400
who dream big.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.690
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.042
for a thousand dollars,
how does that sound?

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.606
- Holy (beep).

00:02:57.606 --> 00:02:58.439
Okay.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.591
- I love you.

00:03:00.591 --> 00:03:01.490
- Thank you.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.763
- Thank you so much.

